Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: add MT7987 MAC and PCS resources

Port the MT7987 MAC, QDMA v3.1 and SGMII routing support to the Linux
6.18 Ethernet driver. Include the required GDM selection and GMAC3 path
rather than depending on the downstream platform PCS conversion.

The Ethernet node uses mediatek,sgmiisys indexed by MAC number. Sparse
zero entries are accepted. Each referenced MT7987 syscon owns clocks
named sgmii_sel, sgmii_tx and sgmii_rx, its optional resets property and
optional mediatek,phya_trx_ck. The MAC driver owns reset/clock acquisition,
enabling and error/remove unwind. No pcs-handle or PCS platform child is
used. E87N uses slot 0 for its external 2500base-x MAC; MAC1 is internal.
Include the downstream idle-FSM check and FE recovery when changing
GMAC2/3 from XGDM to GDM, and update mux bits per MAC.

Do not register WED on MT7987: the MT7988 WED v3 resource layout does
not describe this SoC's single WDMA. Wireless offload is outside this
port. Existing SoCs retain their original queue and clock behaviour.

Base: Linux 6.18.51 (f6388029ea9e2c9e807d73827658738ea131faee).
Derived from the existing E87N Linux 6.12 MT7987 patches and their
required SGMII routing support. No hardware validation is claimed.

